    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1097">

                <pb facs="0814" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.63/300</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Parker,
                        representing American interests, to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-11-21T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 21, 1916, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>575. Department’s 560, November 18, 5 p.m. <hi rendition="#italic">El
                        Democrata</hi> of 15th instant published circular of Fomento Department
                    extending term until February 14th next for the operation of mines.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Parker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
